{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"2914903b1db90af4","type":"text","text":"Agent Creation params\n- model object \n\t- can be either created via using new OpenAI as mentioned in \n\t- Open AI integration via Strands https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/model-providers/openai/\n\t- can be created via using new BedrockModel as mentioned in\n\t- https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/quickstart/typescript/#amazon-bedrock-default\n\t- Google also has a way but ignoring for now\n\t- ","x":-125,"y":-40,"width":605,"height":420},
		{"id":"215a73c53bb3de9b","type":"text","text":"## Not supported in TS\n---\n- Callback handlers https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/streaming/callback-handlers/\n- community tools https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/community-tools-package/\n- Loading tools from files https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/#loading-tools-from-files\n- Concurrent invocations https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/agents/agent-loop/#concurrent-invocations\n- direct tool calling https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/agents/state/#direct-tool-calling\n- ","x":1410,"y":-159,"width":470,"height":579},
		{"id":"c60ef072da9ae1a8","type":"text","text":"## non streaming response\n---\nAgent will return simple JSON response instead of streaming\n\nexample :\n```js\nconst result = await agent.invoke('What is the square root of 144?')\n\nconsole.log(agent.messages)\n```","x":-1320,"y":-330,"width":660,"height":500},
		{"id":"ac9d76eb22160c8b","type":"text","text":"**AgentStreamEvent event types**\ndocs https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/streaming/#event-types\n\nusages :\n https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/streaming/async-iterators/#agentic-loop","x":-2080,"y":755,"width":520,"height":200},
		{"id":"3c14c5ec6aa634ba","type":"text","text":"Disabling Agent console output \nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/quickstart/typescript/#console-output","x":-2302,"y":-249,"width":444,"height":90},
		{"id":"ffc1c175616581be","type":"text","text":"### llms.txt\nhttps://llmstxt.org/\nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/build-with-ai/#raw-markdown-convention","x":2020,"y":170,"width":340,"height":170},
		{"id":"36b5102afe6a5e22","type":"text","text":"Guide to writing secure tools https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/safety-security/responsible-ai/","x":-1340,"y":1436,"width":456,"height":79},
		{"id":"24ac88b259fdebb5","type":"text","text":"### Base Tool schema \n---\nfunction based with zod\n\n```ts\nconst weatherTool = tool({\n  name: 'weather_forecast',\n  description: 'Get weather forecast for a city',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    city: z.string().describe('The name of the city'),\n    days: z.number().default(3).describe('Number of days for the forecast'),\n  }),\n  callback: (input) => {\n    return `Weather forecast for ${input.city} for the next ${input.days} days...`\n  },\n})\n```\n\nrequired things are\n`name`\n`description`\n`inputSchema`\n\n`callback` : method ","x":-1112,"y":1680,"width":640,"height":665},
		{"id":"b1ed2dfe253d6235","type":"text","text":"### Tools without zod and only JSON schema\n\n---\n```ts\nconst weatherTool = tool({\n  name: 'weather_forecast',\n  description: 'Get weather forecast for a city',\n  inputSchema: {\n    type: 'object',\n    properties: {\n      city: { type: 'string', description: 'The name of the city' },\n      days: { type: 'number', description: 'Number of days for the forecast' },\n    },\n    required: ['city'],\n  },\n  callback: (input) => {\n    const { city, days = 3 } = input as { city: string; days?: number }\n    return `Weather forecast for ${city} for the next ${days} days...`\n  },\n})\n```","x":-1760,"y":2400,"width":560,"height":600},
		{"id":"fc4a2532afa50107","type":"text","text":"Tool names must match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$` and be 1 to 64 characters long. Names that do not match this format are replaced with `INVALID_TOOL_NAME` on assistant messages before they are sent to the model, so the request still succeeds but the model can no longer reference the original name.","x":-2040,"y":1760,"width":560,"height":160},
		{"id":"b7bd6bf8f7bf5e8c","type":"text","text":"### Writing methods in async\n---\nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/custom-tools/#async-invocation\n\nclass based tools\nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/custom-tools/#example-with-multiple-tools-in-a-class","x":-1112,"y":2640,"width":367,"height":226},
		{"id":"a9e12311e3393430","type":"text","text":"### Tool Context\n---\nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/custom-tools/#toolcontext","x":-647,"y":2640,"width":327,"height":226},
		{"id":"af580cfbb54fa2d3","type":"text","text":"### creating a MCP server\nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/mcp-tools/#implementing-an-mcp-server\n\nMCP elicitation\nhttps://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/client/elicitation","x":4,"y":2631,"width":316,"height":169},
		{"id":"d0bfc474fb161946","type":"text","text":"## Agent Loop Stop reasons https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/agents/agent-loop/#stop-reasons\n\n```ts\nconst agent = new Agent()\n\n// Cancel after 30 seconds\nsetTimeout(() => agent.cancel(), 30_000)\n\nconst result = await agent.invoke('Analyze this large dataset')\n\nif (result.stopReason === 'cancelled') {\n  console.log('Agent was cancelled due to timeout')\n}\n```\n\nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/agents/agent-loop/#cancellation AGENT DISCONNECT OR CANCEL  on connection fails, can be used in finally blocks\n\n## Common problems in Agent Loop\nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/agents/agent-loop/#common-problems\n","x":720,"y":170,"width":648,"height":882},
		{"id":"e1e427b0046f0d68","type":"text","text":"## multi agent patterns","x":355,"y":1476,"width":250,"height":210},
		{"id":"eee442625ee329c5","type":"text","text":"## Tools\n\nbase : https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/\nDirect tool calling https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/#direct-method-calls -- tools called programatically\n\nTool Executors with multi tools output by agent https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/executors/\n\nCustom tools https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/#1-custom-tools\n\nModule based tools https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/#module-based-tools\n\nmodule base in python https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/#module-based-tools\n\nusing MCP as tools https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/mcp-tools/\n\n### Best Practices \nhttps://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/concepts/tools/#module-based-tools","x":-425,"y":700,"width":600,"height":660},
		{"id":"5d7b158491db12aa","type":"text","text":"## Streaming response\n---\nWhether to change from this to SSE can be decided later\ninstead of `agent.invoke` here we have `agent.stream`\nhere's a sample example\n\n```ts\nasync function handleStreamRequest(req: any, res: any) {\n\nconsole.log(`Got Request: ${JSON.stringify(req.body)}`)\n\nconst { prompt } = req.body as PromptRequest\n\nres.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/x-ndjson')\n\nconst agent = new Agent({\n\ntools: [notebook],\n\nprinter: false,\n\n})\n\nfor await (const event of agent.stream(prompt)) {\n\n// Events automatically serialize to compact JSON via toJSON().\n\n// Only relevant data fields are included — the full Agent instance,\n\n// Tool classes, and mutable hook flags (cancel/retry) are excluded.\n\nres.write(`${JSON.stringify(event)}\\n`)\n\n}\n\nres.end()\n\n}\n```\n\nlater this will be attached to a route in express app","x":-1360,"y":445,"width":700,"height":510}
	],
